{
  "statement": "I acknowledge the concerns raised regarding energy consumption and performance optimization. However, security and privacy must remain paramount. The requirements TRU-01 and TRU-02 may introduce computational overhead, potentially conflicting with energy efficiency (GRN-01) and real-time monitoring (EFF-04). I propose a synthesis where we can implement lightweight encryption methods during critical maneuvers to balance security needs with performance. Additionally, I support the idea of relaxing smoothness constraints (SAF-07) during emergencies, but we must ensure that security measures are not compromised in the process.",
  "conflicts_raised": [
    {
      "ids": ["TRU-01", "GRN-07"],
      "type": "resource",
      "description": "Implementing end-to-end data encryption (TRU-01) may require additional computational resources, potentially conflicting with minimizing energy usage during critical failures (GRN-07)."
    },
    {
      "ids": ["TRU-02", "EFF-04"],
      "type": "logical",
      "description": "Enforcing role-based access control (TRU-02) may introduce latency that conflicts with the requirement for real-time monitoring of ODD compliance (EFF-04)."
    }
  ],
  "positions": [
